---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const lastUpdated = '17 May 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Pixscaler"
  description="Terms of use for the Pixscaler client-side image tool and website."
>
  <article class="legal-page section">
    <div class="container container--narrow prose">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__date">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        By using the Pixscaler website, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not
        use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What Pixscaler is</h2>
      <p>
        Pixscaler is a free, open-source tool for resizing and compressing images in your browser.
        Processing uses Web Workers and canvas APIs on your device. The image content you process is
        not sent to us as part of that workflow.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You may use Pixscaler only with images you have the right to process. You are responsible
        for complying with copyright and other laws that apply to you.
      </p>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the site in a way that is unlawful or infringes someone else’s rights.</li>
        <li>Attempt to disrupt the site or overload it (for example with abusive automated traffic).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. No warranties</h2>
      <p>
        Pixscaler is provided <strong>as is</strong>, without warranties of any kind, to the fullest
        extent allowed by law. We do not guarantee that output files will meet any third-party
        requirement (size, format, dimensions), that every browser will support every feature, or
        that the site will always be available.
      </p>
      <p>
        Always verify results yourself before submitting files to government portals, employers,
        shops, or other services.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the project maintainers and contributors
        are not liable for any damages arising from your use of Pixscaler or this website, including
        indirect or consequential damages or loss of data.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The website is delivered through
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare</a>.
        Your use of the site is also subject to Cloudflare’s terms and policies where they apply to
        visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Open source</h2>
      <p>
        Source code is published on
        <a href="https://github.com/27bhd/Pixscaler" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          GitHub
        </a>
        under the MIT Licence. The exact grant of rights is in the <code>LICENSE</code> file in the
        repository root. If you fork or reuse the code, read that file first.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. When we do, we will change the date at the top of this page.
        Continued use of the site after an update means you accept the revised terms.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about these terms, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:contact@pixscaler.com">contact@pixscaler.com</a>
        or see the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <hr class="divider" />
      <p>
        <a href="/">Back to Pixscaler →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section { padding-block: 3.5rem; }
  .legal-page__date { color: var(--text-faint); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
</style>
